  "notes": "Crawford elects two Republican committee people per precinct, without gender distinction, for four-year terms (county notice). Contest: 'Local Republican Committeepeople', vote for 2. A seat is 'filled' when a printed (party-labelled) ballot candidate received votes, 'empty' when no candidate and no write-in votes were recorded, and 'unknown' when write-in votes were cast, since the results do not show whether a write-in qualified or accepted. Every Crawford contest recorded at least one write-in vote, so no seat is classified 'empty'; most are 'unknown'. Appointments after the primary are not reflected. The official results contain no Republican committee contest for Conneautville Boro (the Democratic committee contests for that precinct are present); its two seats are recorded as 'unknown'."
